From: Nick Kaaz <nk6352@stellar-intel.princeton.edu>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 15:41:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20Central=5Fobject.dilution=5Ffactor=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?to=20decouple=20L=20from=204=CF=80R=C2=B2=CF=83T=E2=81=B4?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- setup_star_bh.c: read new pf parameter Central_object.dilution_factor
  (default 1.0 preserves stock bare-BB behaviour). Fold W into
  geo.lum_star = W * 4πR²σT⁴ so the band-luminosity sum is reduced
  consistently while T continues to set the spectral shape.
- photon_gen.c: in star_init, scale the integrated-Planck flux by
  geo.lum_star_init / (4πR²σT⁴_init) so per-band emission picks up
  the same dilution. Stock W=1 is a no-op.

Lets the central source act as a diluted BB representing (e.g.) a deep
diffusion layer where T sets the colour but the emerging luminosity is
sub-Eddington — needed for super-Eddington outflow models where the
photosphere is well below 4πR²σT⁴.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/photon_gen.c    | 5 +++++
 source/setup_star_bh.c | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/photon_gen.c b/source/photon_gen.c
index b6942f3e..cc81b74d 100644
--- a/source/photon_gen.c
+++ b/source/photon_gen.c
@@ -855,6 +855,11 @@ star_init (freqmin, freqmax, ioniz_or_extract, f)
 
   *f = emit;                    // Calculate the surface flux between freqmin and freqmax
   *f *= (4. * PI * r * r);
+  /* Apply dilution factor implicit in lum_star_init: W = lum_star_init / (4πR²σT⁴_init).
+   * For bare BB (stock Central_object.dilution_factor = 1.0) this ratio is 1 and
+   * *f is unchanged. For W < 1 the band luminosity is reduced by the same factor. */
+  if (geo.tstar_init > 0.0)
+    *f *= geo.lum_star_init / (4. * PI * geo.rstar * geo.rstar * STEFAN_BOLTZMANN * pow (geo.tstar_init, 4.));
 
 
   return (0);
diff --git a/source/setup_star_bh.c b/source/setup_star_bh.c
index c43d3e29..34afe4de 100644
--- a/source/setup_star_bh.c
+++ b/source/setup_star_bh.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ double
 get_stellar_params ()
 {
   char answer[LINELENGTH];
+  double w_dilute = 1.0;
 
   rdpar_comment ("Parameters for the Central Object");
 
@@ -117,7 +118,10 @@ get_stellar_params ()
     }
 
     if (geo.star_radiation)
+    {
       rddoub ("Central_object.temp", &geo.tstar_init);
+      rddoub ("Central_object.dilution_factor", &w_dilute);
+    }
   }
   else
   {
@@ -129,7 +133,10 @@ get_stellar_params ()
 
   geo.tstar = geo.tstar_init;
 
-  geo.lum_star = geo.lum_star_init = 4 * PI * geo.rstar * geo.rstar * STEFAN_BOLTZMANN * pow (geo.tstar, 4.);
+  /* dilution factor decouples L from 4πR²σT⁴: default 1.0 preserves bare-BB;
+   * W<1 lets T set the emission spectrum while L is reduced, so the source
+   * acts as a diluted BB representing (e.g.) a deep diffusion layer */
+  geo.lum_star = geo.lum_star_init = w_dilute * 4 * PI * geo.rstar * geo.rstar * STEFAN_BOLTZMANN * pow (geo.tstar, 4.);
 
 
   /* Describe the secondary if that is required */
